$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: GENERAL PROCEDURE To a solution of 14 mmol of
compound 2 and 35 mmol (2.5 eq) of potassium carbonate dissolved in 27 ml
of N,N-dimethylformamide, 1 g of MSH is added every quarter of an hour,
until all the precursor has disappeared. The temperatures are indicated
in the Table. The mixture is poured into 500 ml of ice cold water. The
precipitate formed is then filtered, washed with water and dried in a
steam room at 100°C. Ethyl
1-amino-7-methoxy-4-oxo-1,4-dihydro-3-quinolinecarboxylate (2c), yield
100%. IR (KBr): 3480, 1710, 1605 cm-1; 1H NMR : δ 1.23 (t, 3H, J= 7.0 Hz,
OCH2CH3 ), 3.87 (s, 3H, OCH3), 4.17 (q, 2H, J= 7.0 Hz, OCH2CH3), 6.41 (s,
2H, NH2), 7.05 (dd, 1H, J= 3.2, 9.0 Hz, H-6), 7.43 (d, 1H, J= 3.2 Hz,
H-8), 8.09 (d, 1H, J= 9.0 Hz, H-5), 8.54 (s, 1H, H-2) ppm; HRMS : m/z
calcd for C13H14N2O4 (M+) 262.2646. found 261.9761.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A convenient procedure for N-amination of 4-oxo-1,4-dihydroquinolines
