$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM B. General Procedure forRu-Catalyzed IntramolecularAmination of C-H Bonds
of ortho-Arylphenylazides. The required arylazides were prepared by
diazotization of the corresponding anilines, all commercially available,
followed by treatment with sodium azide, according to a standard
procedure.33Amixture of azide and RuCl3 • 3H2O in a molar ratio of 100:3
in 3 mL of DME was stirred at 85 °C for 5 h to give a deep brown
solution. The completion of the reaction was indicated by TLC. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, the solvent was
evaporated under vacuum, and the residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography using hexane-EtOAc (12:1, v/v) as the eluant to
afford the product. The product was recrystallized from hexane-EtOAc.
Synthesis and Characterization of 2a. Azide 1a (195 mg, 1 mmol), RuCl3 •
3H2O (8.1 mg, 0.03 mmol). Yield of 2a (white solid), 150 mg (90%). The
spectroscopic data match those reported by Sapi et al.34 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CD3COCD3): δ 10.33 (br, 1 H), 8.15 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 2 H), 7.54 (d, J=7.6
Hz, 2 H), 7.43 (t, J=7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.22 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H). 13C{1H} NMR
(100 MHz, CD3COCD3): δ 139.9, 125.3, 122.8, 119.7, 118.5, 110.6. MS
(ESI): m/z 168.0813 ([M + H] +).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on catalyst,solvent,temperature, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Amination Reactions of Aryl- and
Vinylazides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shou, Wang Ge; Li, Juan; Guo, Tongxun; Lin, Zhenyang; Jia, Guochen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2009), 28(24), 6847-6854

