$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Cp*M(III)-Catalyzed C-H Amination (Table 1 and
2, and Equations 1 and 2) To a screw capped vial equipped with a spinvane
triangular-shaped Teflon stirbar were added benzamide 1 (0.25 mmol), R’N3
2 (0.35 mmol), catalyst [Cp*MCl2]2 (M = Co, Rh, Ir) (0.01 mmol), AgSbF6
(13.7 mg, 0.04 mmol), and 1,1,2,2-TCE-d 2 (0.5 ml) under atmospheric
conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred in a pre-heated oil bath at
an indicated temperature for 1.5 h or 24 h. The reaction was cooled to
room temperature, to which 1,4-dioxane (10.8 μl, 0.13 mmol) as internal
standard was added. This reaction mixture was directly subject to 1H NMR
spectroscopy to determine a crude NMR yield. The authentic NMR data of
all amination products 3 formed in this study except the product 3d and
3f were previously reported and thus utilized here to calculate the NMR
yield of product 3 from the crude reaction mixture. Trace amounts of
R’NH2 derived from the employed azide R’N3 during the catalysis was often
observed depending on reaction conditions by 1H NMR spectroscopy.
N-tert-Butyl-2-(3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)benzoylamino)benzamide (Table 1,
3d) Isolated yield = 87% (white solid). m.p. 153-155°C; 1H NMR (600 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 12.63 (s, 1H), 8.74 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 8.50 (s, 2H), 8.05 (s,
1H), 7.53 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (t, J = 7.6
Hz, 1H), 6.18 (s, 1H), 1.51 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.9,
162.4, 139.2, 137.2, 132.6, 132.6, 132.4, 132.2, 132.0, 127.8, 126.4,
125.7, 125.2, 125.2, 125.2, 125.1, 123.9, 123.5, 122.1, 121.6, 121.5,
120.3, 52.5, 28.7; IR (cm-1) 3337, 2977, 2922, 1670, 1592, 1530, 1519,
1443, 1373, 1277, 1247, 1185, 1120, 904, 752; High Resolution MS (ESI):
calculated for C20H18F6N2O2 [M+Na]+ : 455.1170, found: 455.1182.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst, 87% isolated yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Comparative investigations of Cp*-based Group 9 metal-catalyzed direct
C-H amination of benzamides
