$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Cp*M(III)-Catalyzed
C-H Amination (Table 1 and 2, and Equations 1 and 2) To a screw capped
vial equipped with a spinvane triangular-shaped Teflon stirbar were added
benzamide 1 (0.25 mmol), R’N3 2 (0.35 mmol), catalyst [Cp*MCl2]2 (M = Co,
Rh, Ir) (0.01 mmol), AgSbF6 (13.7 mg, 0.04 mmol), and 1,1,2,2-TCE-d 2
(0.5 ml) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred
in a pre-heated oil bath at an indicated temperature for 1.5 h or 24 h.
The reaction was cooled to room temperature, to which 1,4-dioxane (10.8
μl, 0.13 mmol) as internal standard was added. This reaction mixture was
directly subject to 1H NMR spectroscopy to determine a crude NMR yield.
The authentic NMR data of all amination products 3 formed in this study
except the product 3d and 3f were previously reported and thus utilized
here to calculate the NMR yield of product 3 from the crude reaction
mixture. Trace amounts of R’NH2 derived from the employed azide R’N3
during the catalysis was often observed depending on reaction conditions
by 1H NMR spectroscopy.
N-tert-Butyl-2-(3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)benzoylamino)benzamide (Table 1,
3d) Entry: 2. Product: 3a; Yield: 93%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Comparative investigations of Cp*-based Group 9 metal-catalyzed direct
C-H amination of benzamides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Figg, Travis M.; Park, Sehoon; Park, Juhyeon; Chang, Sukbok; Musaev,
Djamaladdin G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2014), 33(15), 4076-4085

