$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1. General Procedure for the Ir-Catalyzed Amination of Benzamides with
Anilines To a screw capped vial with a spinvane triangular-shaped Teflon
stir bar were added benzamide (0.20 mmol), aniline (0.21 mmol),
IrCp*(OAc)2 (9.0 mg, 0.02 mmol, 10 mol %), AgNTf2 (232 mg, 0.60 mmol, 3.0
equiv), Cu(OAc)2 (18.1 mg, 0.10 mmol, 50 mol %) and 1,2-dichloroethane
(0.66 mL) under atmospheric conditions. The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 24 h, filtered through a pad of celite and then
diluted by adding CH2Cl2 (10 mL)and 3 M aqueous NH3solution.The two
layers were separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2
(10 mLx 3). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4, filtered,
and concentrated in vacuo.And the residue was purified by chromatography
on silica gel (n-hexane/EtOAc or n-hexane/EtOAc/CH2Cl2 or
n-hexane/CH2Cl2) to give the desired product.
N-Adamanty2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenylamino]benzamide, colorless solid,
yield 85%. m.p. 170-172 °C; 1H NMR(600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.41 (s, 1H), 7.50
(d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (dd, J= 16.0, 8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.30 (t, J= 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.21 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 2H), 6.86 (t, J= 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.84 (s, 1H), 2.11
