$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. General Procedure forRu-Catalyzed
IntramolecularAmination of C-H Bonds of ortho-Arylphenylazides. The
required arylazides were prepared by diazotization of the corresponding
anilines, all commercially available, followed by treatment with sodium
azide, according to a standard procedure.33Amixture of azide and RuCl3 •
3H2O in a molar ratio of 100:3 in 3 mL of DME was stirred at 85 °C for 5
h to give a deep brown solution. The completion of the reaction was
indicated by TLC. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature,
the solvent was evaporated under vacuum, and the residue was purified by
silica gel column chromatography using hexane-EtOAc (12:1, v/v) as the
eluant to afford the product. The product was recrystallized from
hexane-EtOAc. Synthesis and Characterization of 2a. Synthesis and
Characterization of 2d. Azide 1d (177 mg, 0.5 mmol), RuCl3 • 3H2O (4.0
mg, 0.015 mmol). Yield of 2d (colorless solid), 148 mg (91%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CD3COCD3): δ 10.68 (br, 1 H), 8.32 (d, J=1.2 Hz, 1 H), 8.19 (d,
J=8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.77 (d, J=1.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.65 (t, J=8.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.50
(t, J=7.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.28 (t, J=7.6 Hz, 1 H). 13C{1H} NMR (100 MHz,
CD3COCD3): δ 140.3, 137.2,129.3, 127.0, 125.7, 122.1, 121.9, 120.7,
119.8, 111.5, 110.6, 104.0, MS (ESI): m/z 326.8936 ([M + H] + ).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Amination Reactions of Aryl- and
Vinylazides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
