$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The anodic oxidation was carried out using an H-type divided cell (4G
glass filter) equipped with an anode consisting of fine fibers made from
carbon felt (Nippon Carbon JF-20-P7, ca. 160 mg, dried at 300 °C/1 mmHg
for 4 hours before use) and a platinum plate cathode (10 mm × 10 mm). In
the anodic chamber was placed a solution of ethyl
2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-3-(4-nitrophenyl)propanoate (32) (0.20 mmol) and
pyridine (0.5 mL) in 0.3 M Bu4NBF4/CH3CN (10.0 mL). In the cathodic
chamber were placed trifluoromethanesulfonic acid (200 μL) and 0.3 M
Bu4NBF4/CH3CN (10.0 mL). The constant current electrolysis (8.0 mA) was
carried out at 25 °C with magnetic stirring. After 3.5 F mol-1 of
electricity was consumed, the reaction mixture was transferred to a
round-bottom flask and was evaporated. Then, piperidine (200 μL, 2.0
mmol) and CH3CN (10 mL) were added to the reaction mixture. The resulting
mixture was stirred at 80 °C for 12 hours. After removal of the solvent
under reduced pressure, the crude product was purified with flash
chromatography. The product was determined by a NOE analysis. ethyl
2-(3-amino-4-methoxyphenyl)-3-(4-nitrophenyl)propanoate (31). Yield:
(61.2 mg, 89%) as pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.14 (t, J
= 7.0 Hz, 3H), 3.08 (dd, J = 14.0, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.46 (dd, J = 13.6, 8.4
Hz, 1H), 3.62-3.73 (m, 3H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 3.98-4.14 (m, 2H), 6.57 (dd, J
= 8.0, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 6.66-6.71 (m, 2H), 7.27 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 8.08 (d,
J = 8.8 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 14.0, 39.5, 52.3, 55.4,
60.9, 110.18, 113.9, 117.8, 123.4, 129.8, 130.3, 136.3, 146.5, 146.7,
147.1, 173.1; HRMS (ESI): [M+H]+ calcd. for C18H21N2O5, 345.1445; found,
345.1440.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, electrochemical (3.5 Faraday per mole), regioselective,
constant current=8mA, fibers made from carbon felt used as anode and
platinum plate used as cathode, H-type cell containing solution of
aromatic substrate, pyridine, Bu4NBF4 and acetonitrile placed in anodic
chamber and solution of trifluoromethanesulfonic acid, Bu4NBF4 and
acetonitrile placed in cathodic chamber used, mechanism studied, key
intermediate for synthesis of VLA-4 antagonist
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Electrochemical C-H Amination: Synthesis of Aromatic Primary Amines via
N-Arylpyridinium Ions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Morofuji, Tatsuya; Shimizu, Akihiro; Yoshida, Jun-ichi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(13), 5000-5003

