$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Amination Procedure. Diethyl
1-Amino-3-methylpyrrole-2,4-dicarboxylate (3a). Method A. To a solution
of pyrrole 2a (1 mmol) in DMF (2 mL) was added NaH (1.2 mmol), and the
reaction was stirred for 45 min at room temperature. NH2Cl (8 mL, ca.
0.15 M in ether) was added via syringe while maintaining a nitrogen
sparge. The reaction was monitored by HPLC until completion. The reaction
was then quenched with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3, diluted with water, and
extracted into ether. Ethyl
1-Amino-2-(n-propylcarboxamido)-3-methylpyrrole-4-carboxylate (3e). 89%
yield. Time (h) 0.5. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33 (s, 1H), 6.05 (br s,
1H), 4.18 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 3.33 (q, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 2.47 (s, 3H),
1.57 (m, 2H), 1.26 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H), 0.93 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 164.9, 162.6, 130.5, 123.8, 123.1, 111.4, 60.0, 41.5,
23.4, 14.8, 12.2, 11.9; MS (ESI) m/z 254.1 (M + H), calcd for C12H19N3O3
253.1. Anal. Calcd for C12H19N3O3: C, 56.90; H, 7.56; N, 16.59. Found: C,
57.07; H, 7.50; N, 16.36.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM N-Amination of pyrrole and indole heterocycles with monochloramine
(NH2Cl)
