$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Deuteration study in the presence of Fe(NO3)3·9H2O. Two identical
reactions were set up. N-(2-deuteriophenyl)-2-aminopyridine 1a-D (0.5
mmol), Cu(OAc)2 (50 mol%), Fe(NO3)3·9H2O (10 mol%), PivOH (2.5 mmol), and
DMF (1.0 mL) were added to a two necked flask in turn. The solution was
stirred at 130 °C for 2 h and 18 h under balloon pressure of O2. After
cooling to room temperature, distilled water (10 mL), triethylamine (1.0
mL), and EtOAc (10 mL) were added to the reaction mixture. The organic
phase was separated, and the aqueous phase was further extracted with
EtOAc (3 × 10 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4 and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
to provide the desired product 2a-D. Yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Direct Intramolecular C-H Amination Reaction Cocatalyzed by Copper(II)
and Iron(III) as Part of an Efficient Route for the Synthesis of
Pyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazoles from N-Aryl-2-aminopyridines
