$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure of Pd(II)-Catalyzed Amination of C-H Bonds: In a 20 mL
seal tube, 2-pyridinesulfonyl-protected phenethylamine derivatives 1a-1o
(0.2 mmol, 1 equiv), Pd(OAc)2 (4.5 mg, 0.1 equiv), PhI(OAc)2 (129 mg, 2
equiv) were dissolved in 20 mL dry toluene under air. The tube was sealed
with a Teflon lined cap, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 130 °C
for 4 h. After cooled to room temperature, the mixture was concentrated
under vacuum and the residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel with a gradient eluent of hexane and ethyl acetate. The
corresponding products. Product: 2a. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.60 (d, J
= 4.4 Hz, 1H), 7.96 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.82 (dt, J 1 = 1.6 Hz, J 2 =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.40-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.02-7.11 (m, 2H), 6.91-6.95 (m, 1H),
4.33 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 3.05 (t, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 156.2, 150.1, 141.5, 137.7, 131.9, 127.4, 127.0, 125.0, 123.6,
123.0, 114.5, 51.3, 28.0; HRMS (ESI-TOF) calcd. for C13H13N2O2S ([M+H]+):
261.0692, Found: 261.0695.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study (optimized on oxidant and solvent), sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Indolines via Pd(II)-Catalyzed Amination of C-H Bonds Using
PhI(OAc)2 as the Bystanding Oxidant
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mei, Tian-Sheng; Leow, Dasheng; Xiao, Han; Laforteza, Brian N.; Yu,
Jin-Quan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(12), 3058-3061

