$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure E: Synthesis of Indoline-2-Carboxylate. A mixture of
MIA-phenylalanin-derivates (0.5 mmol, 1.0 eq), Pd(OAc)2 (5.6 mg, 0.025
mmol, 0.05 eq), F+ (1-Fluoro-2,4,6-trimethylpyridinium Tetrafluoroborate)
source (170.0 mg, 0.75 mmol, 1.5 eq), dry DMF (48.2 μl, 1.25 eq) and dry
DCE (4 mL) in a 10 mL high pressure flask vial (purged with Ar, sealed
with PTFE cap) was heated at 110 °C for 8 hours. The reaction mixture was
cooled to room temperature, and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
residue was purified by silica gel flash chromatography using 10-20%
ethyl acetate in hexanes. The indoline product. 10a: Light yellow solid
(121.6 mg, 88% yield). R f = 0.39, hexane/EtOAc = 2:1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400
MHz): δ = 8.25 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.23 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.16 (d, J
= 7.6 Hz, 1H), 7.05 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 5.50-5.48 (m, 1H), 3.92 (s, 3H),
3.70 (s, 3H), 3.57 (dd, J = 16.4, 11.2 Hz, 1H), 3.21-3.17 (m, 1H), 2.07
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ = 172.5, 163.5, 152.6, 143.1, 129.2,
127.9, 124.6, 124.1, 117.9, 62.5, 52.6, 33.6, 11.8; ESI-HRMS Calcd for
C14H17N2O4 + [M+H+]: 277.1183; Found: 277.1181. [α]27 D = -69.1 (CHCl3, c
= 1.0).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed high-pressure flask used, optimized on catalyst loading, additive
and solvent, inert atmosphere, reaction under air gave lower yield,
optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Assembly of Indoline-2-carboxylate-Embodied Dipeptides via Pd-Catalyzed
C(sp2)-H Bond Direct Functionalization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM He, Yu-Peng; Zhang, Chao; Fan, Mengyang; Wu, Zhijie; Ma, Dawei
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(3), 496-499

