$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: D. General Procedure for Ru-Catalyzed
Intramolecular Amination of C-H Bonds of 2-Azido-3-arylacrylates 5. A
mixture of azide (1 mmol) and RuCl3 • 3H2O (0.03 mmol) in 3mL of DME in a
sealed tube in an oil bath at 105 °C was stirred for 3 h to give a deep
brown solution. The completion of the reaction was indicated by TLC. The
reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, the solvent was
evaporated under vacuum, and the residual oil was purified by silica gel
column chromatography using hexane-EtOAc (13:1, v/v) as the eluant to
afford the product. The product was recrystallized from hexane-EtOAc.
Synthesis and Characterization of 6a Synthesis and Characterization of
6c. Azide 5c 44 (247 mg, 1 mmol),RuCl3 • 3H2O(8.2mg, 0.03 mmol). Yield of
6c (white solid) 193 mg (88%). The spectral data matched those reported
by Cruz et al.47 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3COCD3): δ 10.70 (br, 1 H), 7.58 (d,
J=8.8 Hz, 1 H), 7.13 (s, 1 H), 7.03 (d, J = 1.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.23 (m, 1 H),
4.36 (q, J= 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 3.85 (s, 3 H), 1.37 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3 H).
13C{1H} NMR (100 MHz, CD3COCD3): δ 161.0, 158.5, 138.4, 126.5, 122.6,
121.5, 111.7, 108.0, 93.7, 59.8, 54.5, 13.6. MS (ESI): m/z 220.0952 ([M +
H] + ).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ruthenium-Catalyzed Intramolecular Amination Reactions of Aryl- and
Vinylazides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Shou, Wang Ge; Li, Juan; Guo, Tongxun; Lin, Zhenyang; Jia, Guochen
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2009), 28(24), 6847-6854

